 # Changelog
 
+## 0.3.3
+
+Additive; no breaking changes. New dependency: `rightkit-crypto` 0.1.0 (blake3, serde_json). Not compiled or run here; verification is the main chat's batch.
+
+- **Log file handle for a detached child (rightkit#713, and rightkit#239 follow-up).** `RotatingTextWriter::open_append_file()` and `JsonlStore::open_append_file()` run the open-time and size rotation, then open the current file for append and return the `File`, so it can be a child's stdio (`Stdio::from(file)`). The store honours `with_owner_only` and the cross-process rotation lock. Bytes written through the handle are not scrubbed, counted or rotated while it is open. `rotate_numbered(path, keep)` (re-exported) shifts a file into `path.1` .. `path.keep` on demand and drops the oldest; the caller owns the size check.
+- **Key-token text redactor (rightkit#520).** New `KeyTokenRedactor` (`new`, `with_salt`, `token`, `redact`), `key_token(value, salt)` and `redact_key_values(line, keys)`: the value of each configured `key=value` pair in a text line (for example `account=`, `label=`) becomes `#` plus 16 hex digits (HMAC-SHA256 keyed with the salt, truncated to 8 bytes, via `rightkit-crypto`), stable across lines and platforms; use an app-private secret salt, because an empty or public salt leaves short values guessable. Case-insensitive keys at word starts, quoted values keep their quotes, empty values and existing tokens are left alone (idempotent). `RedactionPolicy` is unchanged.
+- **Family-wide daily clear and warn-and-continue init (rightkit#750).** With feature `tracing`: `clear_tracing_logs(dir, &[prefixes])` deletes every `<prefix>.YYYY-MM-DD.jsonl` of the given prefixes and returns the count (other files untouched; a missing directory is `Ok(0)`). `install_tracing_or_warn(config)` never fails: it warns on stderr and returns the new `TracingGuard::noop()` when setup fails or a global subscriber exists, and `install_stderr_tracing_once(filter)` returns whether it installed. `install_tracing` is unchanged.
+- Unchanged because already present: stderr layer (rightkit#546, `stderr_layer`), rotate-on-open and `stem.N.ext` names (rightkit#239), recording gate and drop-oldest batch cap (rightkit#390 Rust part). The OTLP export half of rightkit#546 stays out (refused by ruling).
+- Tests: `keytext::tests`, `textlog::tests`, `store::tests`, `rotate::tests`, `tracing_file::tests`.
+
 ## 0.3.2 (2026-10-17)
 
 - **URL and OAuth secret text redaction (rightkit#371).** New `redact_url_text(&str) -> String` (re-exported from the crate root): each `scheme://` URL keeps scheme, host and path, loses userinfo and fragment, and a query becomes `?[redacted]`; `name=value` pairs whose name is a known secret parameter (`access_token`, `refresh_token`, `id_token`, `client_secret`, `code`, `state`, `token`, `key`, `password`, and similar) keep the name and the value becomes `[redacted]`. Other text is unchanged. Additive; `RedactionPolicy` and `scrub_text` are unchanged. Tests in `scrub::url_text_tests`. Not compiled or run.
