 # Changelog
 
-## Unreleased
+## 0.1.5
+
+- **Publishes the window crash capture (rightkit#642, rightkit#760).** npm 0.1.4 was published without `crash.ts`; `installWindowCrashCapture`, `scrubWindowCrashText`, `RIGHTKIT_CRASH_WINDOW_ERROR_COMMAND` and their types are exported from the package root in this version (already in the source below). Version bumped so the next publish carries them.
+- **Renderer error capture and persisted ring buffer (rightkit#390, rightkit#760).** `installRendererErrorCapture(client, { surface, target?, storage?, storageKey?, maxEntries?, dedupMs?, now? })` registers window `error` and `unhandledrejection` listeners and logs a content-free `renderer_error` event with `surface`, `kind` (`uncaught` | `rejection`) and `code` (the error name only; no message or stack). The app's `allowedFields` must include `surface`, `kind` and `code`. Repeats of the same kind and code within `dedupMs` (default 1000) are counted, not logged. With `storage` (for example `localStorage`), the newest `maxEntries` (default 50) entries `{ ts_ms, surface, kind, code, count }` persist across reloads; `readRendererErrorRing(storage, key?)` reads them. Idempotent per target; uninstall function returned; never throws into the page. Additive. The Tauri command module and the Rust recording gate and drop-oldest cap are on the `rightkit-logs` side (the Rust cap is in 0.3.2).
+
+Also in 0.1.5 (previously listed as Unreleased):
 
 - Owner gap OG16-5, JavaScript side (additive, nothing installed by default). `installWindowCrashCapture({ invoke, ... })` captures `window` `error` and `unhandledrejection`, scrubs the text (known secrets via `redactValues`, bearer tokens, JWTs, emails, long hex, home paths, URL query and fragment), caps message and stack size, rate-limits (5 per minute, 25 per page by default) and sends one `{ report }` to the app-registered `rightkit_crash_window_error` command (`RIGHTKIT_CRASH_WINDOW_ERROR_COMMAND`). Send failures are swallowed. Rust half: `rightkit-crash` feature `window-errors`.
